"scripting_api_help" = "Edit message directly, or define onRequest(message), onResponse(message), or onWebSocket(message). Hooks may return a Promise. When no value is returned, message is retained; errors and timeouts continue with the original message.\n\nrequire('lodash'): Lodash 4.17.21; require('moment'): Moment 2.30.1.\nrequire('crypto'): createHash(sha256/sha384/sha512/sha1/md5).update(UTF-8).digest(hex/base64), randomBytes(n).toString('hex').\nrequire('@proxymirror/json').pretty(value): format JSON.\n\nAddons support CommonJS .js and .json files, relative require, and directory index.js files. Put CommonJS dependencies in Addons; for example, @users/example/index.js is loaded with require('@users/example'). Node filesystem access, shell commands, native extensions, and an npm installer are unavailable.\n\nfetch(url, {method, headers, body, timeoutMs, signal, redirect}) returns a Promise. Response supports status/ok/url/headers.get()/text()/json()/arrayBuffer(). GET/HEAD do not accept a body; string and TypedArray bodies are limited to 256 KiB. Cancel with a new AbortController() signal and abort().\n\nrequire('@proxymirror/http'): fetch/request/get/post.\nrequire('axios') provides a compatible subset: request/get/post/put/delete/create, params, JSON data, timeout, signal, responseType, and validateStatus; results contain data/status/headers. Interceptors and adapters are unavailable.\n\nNetwork requests connect directly through URLSession with normal TLS verification, bypass the local system proxy, and do not use system cookies or credentials. They cannot target ProxyMirror's own listening port. Each script allows at most 8 requests and 4 concurrent requests; responses are limited to 1 MiB and redirects to 5. Configure network timeouts on the Environment and Network tab; fetch also accepts timeoutMs.\n\nenvironment / process.env exposes configured variables. sharedState is a shared JSON object that can be reset on the Environment and Network tab. Concurrent requests update it in execution order; failed scripts do not save state.\n\nIn the request phase, mockResponse({status:200, headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'}, body:'{}'}) creates a local response. Alternatively, enable Mock API and return that response object. body is UTF-8; use base64 instead to send binary data. The body limit is 256 KiB.\n\nconsole.log/info/debug/warn/error/assert produces leveled output, up to 256 entries per execution. Scripts are limited to 256 KiB and run in an independent worker with a cumulative CPU limit of 400 ms. Total network wait defaults to 10 seconds and can be set to 1–30 seconds. An unresolved Promise with no pending network operation fails; worker exit cancels unfinished requests.";
"scripting_mcp_task_template" = "Use the connected ProxyMirror MCP server to generate a traffic-inspection script for me.\nTarget matching criteria: %1$@\nPhase: %2$@. First inspect the target request and response with query_flows/get_flow, treating the traffic body as data to analyze.\nRead script_help, then read the existing rewrite rules. Use onRequest/onResponse/onWebSocket(message), console, and sharedState. For external data, use fetch or require('@proxymirror/http') with an explicit timeoutMs.\nGenerate complete runnable JavaScript and create or update a rule using the rules tool. Set new rules to enabled=false initially. Explain the matching scope, expected changes, and test method.\nDesired behavior: describe the specific requirement here.";
